---
description: WASS (Web Application Secret Scanner) project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` in the repository root — it is the canonical instruction set for
WASS (product thesis, scope, non-goals, hard safety rules, finding schema, working rules, and the
session bootstrap protocol). Also read `docs/HANDOFF.md` and `docs/TASKS.md` before doing anything,
and record decisions in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.

Highlights (full text in AGENTS.md):
- One milestone at a time; acceptance criteria in docs/TASKS.md. Never expand scope — stop and ask.
- Never build/execute scanned code; no sandboxes. SSRF guards and ownership gating are hard requirements.
- Raw secrets never leave the engine: renderers/exporters/API/LLM accept only `RedactedFinding`.
- Rules are not done until fixtures pass; fixtures use obviously fake values.
- After each task: update docs/TASKS.md, rewrite docs/HANDOFF.md, commit.
